## The account's api tokens

A tab of the profile (symfony-user-ds, `ProfileTabProviderInterface`) at `/account/api-tokens`, for an account that can hold user tokens (symfony-api, `user_token.token_class` set):

- every token of the account: its label, its hint, when it was created, **last used** — « never » until a call signs with it —, when it expires — « never » for none —, and whether it is active, expired or revoked;
- a token issued: a label, an expiration only if one is wanted. Its secret is shown once, on the page the form leads back to, with a button copying it; the page reloaded no longer has it;
- a token revoked from its row, after a confirmation: the clients signing with it are refused from then on.

The tokens are read and changed through symfony-api's `UserTokenService`, as its `/_api/user-tokens` endpoints do; those need not be routed.

## Installation

```php
// config/bundles.php
Wexample\SymfonyApiDs\WexampleSymfonyApiDsBundle::class => ['all' => true],
```

```yaml
# config/routes/….yaml
symfony_api_ds:
    resource: '@WexampleSymfonyApiDsBundle/Controller/'
    type: attribute
```
